  "description": "Raised rates have been on the table for a long time now, but how will that impact the stock market?",
  "body_html": "<p>Most the market seems to just be waiting for a Federal Reserve Interest Rate decisions tomorrow. Though I expect “quiet” today and intraday volatility tomorrow, these decisions have been priced in. Macro trends remain intact. We knew the likelihood of an interest rate hike was high, months ago. And so did the market…</p><p>That is the primary reason I think the market has been so choppy. Remember, <em><strong>the stock market is a forward looking discounting mechanism</strong></em>. If you and I know a piece of information, it is likely the market priced it in already. Its very rare I feel like I know something before the market does. Maybe once a year or so.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!lB1y!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd6dce64f-a979-4e68-8195-89691db8e5c7_1410x825.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!lB1y!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd6dce64f-a979-4e68-8195-89691db8e5c7_1410x825.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!lB1y!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd6dce64f-a979-4e68-8195-89691db8e5c7_1410x825.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!lB1y!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd6dce64f-a979-4e68-8195-89691db8e5c7_1410x825.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!lB1y!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd6dce64f-a979-4e68-8195-89691db8e5c7_1410x825.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!lB1y!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd6dce64f-a979-4e68-8195-89691db8e5c7_1410x825.png\" width=\"1410\" height=\"825\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/d6dce64f-a979-4e68-8195-89691db8e5c7_1410x825.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:825,&quot;width&quot;:1410,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:204350,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/i/215835530?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd6dce64f-a979-4e68-8195-89691db8e5c7_1410x825.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!lB1y!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd6dce64f-a979-4e68-8195-89691db8e5c7_1410x825.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!lB1y!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd6dce64f-a979-4e68-8195-89691db8e5c7_1410x825.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!lB1y!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd6dce64f-a979-4e68-8195-89691db8e5c7_1410x825.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!lB1y!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd6dce64f-a979-4e68-8195-89691db8e5c7_1410x825.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Market appears to have been pricing in raised interest rates for months now. </figcaption></figure></div><p><strong>Someone asked:</strong> “What if the Fed doesn’t raise rates what if they pause?”</p><p>Possible. I consider that the unlikely situation, as CME Forecasts has that at a 7.3% chance at time of writing, and I have never seen CME miss.<a class=\"footnote-anchor\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteAnchorToDOM\" id=\"footnote-anchor-1\" href=\"#footnote-1\" target=\"_self\">1</a> But still possible. The primary reason for keeping rates the same would be the “war” (this administration does not like using the term “war” but we all know that is exactly what it is). Raising rates during “war” is not really optimal for the U.S.. But then again, this administration and the Federal Reserve is full of wild cards and they do not have much of a choice considering inflation. </p><p>Regardless, I think we are still in an optimal situation for the blow off top:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Raise rates:</strong> Market priced this in already. </p></li><li><p><strong>Keep rates the same</strong>: Bullish for the markets, this would be a surprise</p></li><li><p><strong>Lower rates:</strong> Nearly a 0% chance, but this would be a huge surprise and very bullish for the markets. And I would not definitively say this is off the table… Inflation is still rising in the United States.<a class=\"footnote-anchor\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteAnchorToDOM\" id=\"footnote-anchor-2\" href=\"#footnote-2\" target=\"_self\">2</a> </p></li></ul><h4>Regardless of these speculations, we can say some things for certain:</h4><ol><li><p>The Stock Market <em><strong>remains in a well defined bull market</strong></em>. Aside from short term traders, going short is a bad idea, in my opinion. </p></li><li><p>We have not seen any large cap, reputable company “snap” or crash massively in a single day, a huge early bear market signal. </p></li><li><p>We are seeing M2 Money Supply rate of rise increase, a by product of “war”. This normally devalues the dollar, and makes assets (stocks) go up. Normally. </p></li><li><p>We are still finding great stocks to buy. </p><p></p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p></li></ol><p>Though I think the AI sector is undergoing turbulence, “Recession Resistant” stocks keep performing well for us. I picked up a break out health care stock yesterday, you can <strong><a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/flash-update-this-recession-resistant?r=4z8lgl\">check it out here (click)</a>.</strong> </p><p>Keeping today pretty light. If you have any questions, feel free to swing by the <a href=\"https://open.substack.com/chat/posts/eb3f00e6-9f30-4570-8e48-c0bde66e4eec\">Main Chat</a> during market hours. Or just come in and say hi!</p><h4>If you like this content, be sure to LIKE ❤️ and Re-Stack 🔄! This helps combat the AI slop on Substack. </h4><div class=\"captioned-button-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/federal-reserve-interest-rates-tomorrow?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CaptionedButtonToDOM\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">Know someone into investing? Share this post with them!</p></div><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/federal-reserve-interest-rates-tomorrow?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/federal-reserve-interest-rates-tomorrow?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share\"><span>Share</span></a></p></div><div class=\"footnote\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteToDOM\"><a id=\"footnote-1\" href=\"#footnote-anchor-1\" class=\"footnote-number\" contenteditable=\"false\" target=\"_self\">1</a><div class=\"footnote-content\"><p>https://www.cmegroup.com/markets/interest-rates/cme-fedwatch-tool.html</p></div></div><div class=\"footnote\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteToDOM\"><a id=\"footnote-2\" href=\"#footnote-anchor-2\" class=\"footnote-number\" contenteditable=\"false\" target=\"_self\">2</a><div class=\"footnote-content\"><p>https://www.bls.gov/cpi/</p></div></div>",
